rts and cross-engine signals", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "signals.js kinds run on a 15-minute beat with remembered signal_state to avoid re-firing on unchanged findings; PORTFOLIO reserved symbol avoids table rebuild; delivery is in-app only."}, {"id": "readme_briefing", "label": "Briefing (materiality ranking)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "materiality = 100 x strength x stake x kind weight; reports change not state; read-only; verdict can conclude nothing happened."}, {"id": "readme_correlation_engine", "label": "Correlation engine (date-joined)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Joining on date not position: identical prices correlate 1.0 joined on date but -0.04 by position. Null never 0; average linkage avoids chaining."}, {"id": "readme_xray", "label": "Portfolio X-ray (look-through floors)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Yahoo publishes only top ten holdings, so weights are floors; scaling disclosed weights up to 100% would be fabrication."}, {"id": "readme_attribution", "label": "Attribution (Carino-linked, vs own average)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Brinson needs benchmark sector weights no free source provides, so decomposes against the portfolio itself; Carino linking makes parts sum to compounded return exactly."}, {"id": "readme_importer", "label": "Statement importe